  | ^ a `never` function must end every path with `throw` or a call such as `fail(...)`
fix (review): fail at the end of `stop`
7 |   fail(_);

error[E0654]: `quit` returns never, so it can't `return`
  --> never.dat:10:3
10 |   return;
   |   ^^^^^^^ throw an error instead, or change the return type

error[E0252]: a parameter can't have type never
  --> never.dat:13:19
13 | function takes(x: never, y: void): int {
   |                   ^^^^^ no value has this type, so the function could never be called

error[E0252]: a parameter can't have type void
  --> never.dat:13:29
13 | function takes(x: never, y: void): int {
   |                             ^^^^ no value has this type, so the function could never be called
